# The invoice draft tables (ticket #44, D11, D17, D44, D59 (1)). Both are tenant tables under the standard isolation
# policy, audited by trigger, and readable by job handlers (the MyInvois mapping will read the invoice) but never
# writable by them. Approved by Torres on 2026-11-11 as a copy of the item and customer masters' pattern (0036, 0038).
# The rules that must hold whoever writes are kept in the database:
#   - when a signed-in user is in play (`app_user_id()` is set) only the owner and staff of the company may write an
#     invoice or its lines. Operator commands and migrations run with no user;
#   - an invoice never moves to another company, its customer and every line's item belong to its own company, and a
#     line belongs to the invoice's company;
#   - only a draft can be changed or deleted, and only a draft's lines can be added, changed or deleted, so an
#     invoice that has left the draft state stays locked (D17, D19). The approval ticket (#46) lifts this for the one
#     transition it owns.
